<title>BRAZIL: CSN forms group to bid on CVRD -- report.</title>
<headline>CSN forms group to bid on CVRD -- report.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private steelmaker CSN has agreed with four investors to form a consortium to bid at the April 29 privatization auction of Companhia Vale do Rio Doce (CVRD), O Globo newspaper said.</p>
<p>Maria Silvia Bastos Marques, CSN main executive, was quoted by the newspaper as saying CSN's partners will be South Africa's Gencor Ltd, pulp and paper group Suzano, Nations Bank, and the pension fund for Vale's employees Valia.</p>
<p>The newspaper said the formal announcement of the consortium will be made Friday.</p>
<p>At the auction, the CSN consortium will compete with a group led by local cement conglomerate Grupo Votorantim, O Globo said.</p>
<p>((--Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo Newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
